# Development

## Prerequisites<a id="prerequisites"></a>

- [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/), or [nox](https://nox.thea.codes/) with
  [antsibull-nox](https://docs.ansible.com/projects/antsibull-nox/) in one
  Python environment.
- [Podman](https://podman.io/) for the `ansible-test` sanity sessions and the
  container platforms of Molecule. See
  [`extensions/molecule/README.md`](./extensions/molecule/README.md) for
  virtual machines and the execution environment scenario.

## Checks<a id="checks"></a>

Run every check from the collection root, inside its Git repository:

```bash
uv run noxfile.py                 # rewrite, then check: lint, docs, Markdown, changelog, build
CI=true uv run noxfile.py         # check only; fails on anything a rewrite would change
uv run noxfile.py -l              # list all sessions
uv run noxfile.py -s ansible-test-sanity  # ansible-test sanity, one session per ansible-core version
uv run noxfile.py -s molecule     # Molecule, "default" scenario
uv run noxfile.py -s molecule -- test --platform-name molecule-debian13
```

With nox installed, `nox` replaces `uv run noxfile.py`. A plain run applies
the project's own rewrites before checking: `ansible-lint --fix`, role
documentation generated from `meta/argument_specs.yml` and formatted as
`.ansible-docsmith.toml` configures, Markdown formatting.
With `CI=true` every session only checks. Arguments after `--` go to the
session's tool unchanged. `noxfile.py` documents each session; the built-in
sessions are configured in `antsibull-nox.toml`.

If `docs-check` fails with `AF_UNIX path too long` under Python 3.14, run nox
with Python 3.13 or from a shorter checkout path: `antsibull-docs` starts
worker processes whose socket path includes the checkout.

